  <!--
    Tripwire entry for GetLists2013's two masked defects (see GetLists2013.java:98-99).

    - No <d:NoCrawl> element here at all, so GetLists2013 must fall back to its
      default. GetLists2013.java:98 reads NoCrawl from the correct per-entry
      map but defaults to TRUE, where the modern GetLists defaults to FALSE.
      The two entries above always supply NoCrawl explicitly, so that wrong
      default is never exercised.
    - <d:Hidden> is true here, but GetLists2013.java:99 reads Hidden from the
      wrong map (the outer dataMap instead of the per-entry value map), so it
      always falls back to its own default of FALSE - silently wrong for this
      entry once the outer bug below is fixed.

    Today this entry changes nothing: GetLists2013 reads EntityTypeName from
    that same wrong outer map, so entityTypeName is always null and every
    entry - including this one - is skipped, keeping the count at 0 (see
    GetLists2013Test#test_currentBehavior_returnsNoLists, which must keep
    asserting 0). Once the EntityTypeName line is fixed to read from the
    per-entry map, this entry starts being counted, and:
      * if NoCrawl still defaults to TRUE, this entry (no NoCrawl element)
        will be wrongly excluded from crawling;
      * if Hidden still reads from the wrong map, this entry will report
        isHidden()==false despite <d:Hidden>true</d:Hidden>.
    Do not delete this entry when the EntityTypeName bug is fixed - it is
    what makes those two remaining defects visible instead of coincidentally
    passing.
  -->
  <entry>
    <content type="application/xml">
      <m:properties>
        <d:Id m:type="Edm.Guid">44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444</d:Id>
        <d:Title>Hidden No-NoCrawl List</d:Title>
        <d:EntityTypeName>HiddenNoNoCrawlList</d:EntityTypeName>
        <d:BaseTemplate m:type="Edm.Int32">100</d:BaseTemplate>
        <d:Hidden m:type="Edm.Boolean">true</d:Hidden>
        <d:ItemCount m:type="Edm.Int32">0</d:ItemCount>
      </m:properties>
    </content>
  </entry>
